<title>HONG KONG: San Miguel HK 1996 year net up 10.5 pct.</title>
<headline>San Miguel HK 1996 year net up 10.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   49.0	 vs 44.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    4.0	  vs 4.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  115.8 gain vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    183.41     vs 165.91</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,289.51   vs 1,268.47</p>
<p>    Company name		 San Miguel Brewery Hong Kong Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  April 3-8</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   April 14</p>
<p>NOTE - San Miguel Brewery, a subsidiary of San Miguel Corp of the Philippines, is a beer producer.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on provision set aside from the proceeds of the sale of the Sham Tseng Brewery site in 1994 in anticipation of costs which would be incurred in decommissioning the brewery and represents the excess of those provisions over actual costs incurred.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
